THE COUNTRY IS ENDING AGAIN

Matt Goodwin, Tory Recycling and the Industrial Production of Political Alarm

A satirical examination of a political analyst who appears to have become his own research subject

⸻

Abstract

Matt Goodwin has spent a substantial portion of his professional life studying populism, political dissatisfaction, elite distrust, voter behaviour and the mechanisms through which political grievance becomes political mobilisation.

He has subsequently become a Reform UK parliamentary candidate, political campaigner, broadcaster and subscription-funded commentator whose contemporary output includes such formulations as:

“The Tories betrayed Britain.”

“The ongoing destruction of the United Kingdom.”

“Why an obscure local election should TERRIFY the Right…”

His website offers readers “evidence and analysis that challenges the establishment” while inviting more than 90,000 readers to become paid supporters of a political project which Goodwin describes as giving a voice to people ignored by established institutions. (Matt Goodwin)

This presents an unusually convenient research opportunity.

The political scientist has entered the experiment.

This paper examines three connected phenomena.

First, the conversion of ordinary political events into permanent existential emergency.

Second, the tendency for claims of national decline to travel substantially further than the policy mechanisms supposedly capable of reversing it.

Third, the remarkable proposition that Britain was “betrayed” by the Conservative Party and should therefore be rescued by Reform UK — a party whose current parliamentary delegation contains five MPs who were themselves Conservative MPs, while its other three MPs also possess previous Conservative Party histories.

The resulting political model may be summarised as:

[
\text{Conservatives ruined Britain}
]

therefore

[
\text{replace Conservatives}
]

with

[
\text{a surprising number of Conservatives}.
]

The paper names the wider phenomenon the Goodwin Permanent Emergency Machine.

Its primary product is not government.

It is alarm.

