2. Methodology

The methodology employed in this study is intentionally primitive.

Take a Goodwin proposition.

Remove the emotional adjectives.

Identify the factual premise.

Identify the conclusion.

Attempt to locate the mechanism connecting the two.

Where no mechanism is immediately visible, shake the argument gently.

If several references to “betrayal”, “the establishment”, “destruction”, “ordinary people” and imminent catastrophe fall out, record the result.

This method shall be called:

Taking the Argument Seriously

It is surprisingly destructive.

