4. The Obscure Council By-Election Asked to Carry the Entire Nation on Its Back

Goodwin’s August 2026 article concerns a local election.

There is absolutely nothing wrong with analysing local elections.

They can reveal changes in political organisation, tactical voting, turnout and voter coalitions.

Goodwin himself explains that this particular contest might offer lessons about tactical behaviour between political blocs. (Matt Goodwin)

But observe the headline.

The election does not:

suggest an interesting possibility.

It does not:

provide one potentially useful datapoint.

It should:

TERRIFY

the Right.

This is an impressive burden to place upon a council ward.

Somewhere in England, several thousand people go to a community centre, place crosses on pieces of paper and return home to make tea.

By breakfast the result apparently contains information concerning the destiny of Western civilisation.

This is political analysis conducted with the emotional calibration of a smoke detector.

