5. Democracy Is Sacred Until People Vote Incorrectly

One supplied Goodwin post states:

“Imagine looking at the ongoing destruction of the United Kingdom and then celebrating the Greens and Labour winning elections.”

This is worth examining.

Greens and Labour winning elections is inserted as evidence within a description of the:

“ongoing destruction of the United Kingdom.”

Yet elections are not something happening to democracy.

They are democracy doing the thing.

People vote.

Votes are counted.

Candidates win.

Apparently some voters select the wrong answer.

This creates the following asymmetric model:

[
\text{preferred party wins}
\rightarrow
\text{the people have spoken}
]

whereas:

[
\text{opposing party wins}
\rightarrow
\text{Britain is being destroyed}.
]

Democracy remains extremely important, provided the electorate follows the instructions.

