7. The Wonderful Resilience of a Permanent Emergency

The permanent-emergency model has an important advantage.

It is extraordinarily difficult to falsify.

If Reform wins:

THE PEOPLE ARE REVOLTING AGAINST THE ESTABLISHMENT.

If Reform loses:

THE ESTABLISHMENT IS IGNORING THE PEOPLE.

If a poll supports the thesis:

THE SILENT MAJORITY HAS SPOKEN.

If a poll contradicts it:

THE ELITES STILL DON’T UNDERSTAND THE COUNTRY.

If an opponent wins an election:

BRITAIN IS BEING DESTROYED.

This creates what philosophers of science might technically describe as a fucking excellent business model.

No observation requires the theory itself to disappear.

It merely generates tomorrow’s article.

