8. When Claims Encounter Verification

The Gorton and Denton election later became the subject of claims concerning illegal “family voting”.

Greater Manchester Police investigated.

The returning officer’s team independently examined the claims and polling-station records.

Manchester City Council subsequently announced that the allegations were not substantiated and that the integrity of the by-election had not been affected. The returning officer specifically warned against conclusions that were not based upon “factual and verifiable evidence”. (Manchester City Council)

There is something rather old-fashioned about this process.

Claim.

Evidence.

Investigation.

Conclusion.

No capital letters were required.

