19. The Cunt Variable

For methodological transparency, the author wishes to record an additional variable.

The author considers Matt Goodwin:

[
C = \text{a cunt}.
]

This judgement is editorial rather than quantitative and is therefore excluded from the primary regression.

Fortunately, it is not required.

A political argument does not become bad because its author is a cunt.

It becomes bad when:

* the conclusion outruns the evidence;
* emotionally loaded terminology performs the work of causal reasoning;
* counterexamples disappear;
* local observations become sweeping national predictions;
* contrary outcomes are absorbed rather than permitted to falsify the narrative;
* and political advocacy continues presenting itself with the aesthetic authority of disinterested analysis.

Once those defects have been established, Cunt Variable (C) may be reintroduced recreationally.

