21. The Difference Between Analysis and Content

Serious political analysis frequently produces deeply annoying conclusions.

Sometimes the evidence supports your opponent.

Sometimes the effect is small.

Sometimes causation is uncertain.

Sometimes there are five plausible explanations.

Sometimes the correct conclusion is:

We do not yet know.

Political content operates under different incentives.

It benefits from:

certainty.

villains.

betrayal.

urgency.

identity.

And above all:

another episode tomorrow.

The danger is not simply ideological bias.

Bias is ancient.

The more interesting danger is the creation of a political information system in which emotional intensity itself is repeatedly mistaken for analytical depth.

A sentence being furious does not make it explanatory.

